# Code owners.
#
# Scoped to CI/CD definitions, which hold credentials and federate into
# Azure. Application code is intentionally not owned so routine changes
# are unaffected.
#
# Directory patterns are used deliberately: a file-level pattern would
# leave newly added files in the same directory unowned.
#
# CODEOWNERS only auto-requests reviewers. Merge enforcement comes from
# `require_code_owner_review: true` in a ruleset.

/.github/workflows/     @calliora/development
/.github/actions/       @calliora/development

# The policy file itself. Without this, a CODEOWNERS-only PR could strip
# the rules above without owner review, leaving every privileged path
# unowned for any later PR. `.github/CODEOWNERS` outranks root and
# `docs/`, so protecting this single path is sufficient.
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @calliora/development
